WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.084
- All right.
We have Steven Jackson.

00:00:01.084 --> 00:00:02.293
We don't wanna waste
any more time.

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:04.045
Just go.
- All right, so here we go.

00:00:04.045 --> 00:00:05.880
You got two teams. You played
two out of the four teams.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.173
You played the Rams,
the Patriots.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.925
We'll get to the Patriots
in a second.

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:10.510
But first of all,
do you root for the Rams?

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.055
Like, are you a Rams fan
because of your time there?

00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:15.390
- Yeahhh.
- That's a no.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.058
- That was a big breath.
- That was a lean back—

00:00:17.058 --> 00:00:18.852
- You saw that body language?
- Yeah, I did.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.186
That was bad body language.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.896
- It is bad, I know.

00:00:21.896 --> 00:00:23.606
- But you're one of the all-time
greats in Rams history.

00:00:23.606 --> 00:00:25.775
It's you, Dickerson,
and Gurley and Faulk.

00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:27.777
- Well, so wait.
That's where I wanna go.

00:00:27.777 --> 00:00:29.946
- But of course, he's gonna ask
my question now, too

00:00:29.946 --> 00:00:31.614
is, do you—
all right.

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:33.241
So, first of all,
do you root for the Rams?

00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:34.617
Just start there.
- I do.

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:36.661
But I—
it's bittersweet, right?

00:00:36.661 --> 00:00:38.413
- Yeah?
- It's like, you give them

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:39.998
almost a decade, nine years

00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:41.499
you give them
everything you have.

00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:43.126
Never better than 8-8.

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:45.045
- Right.
- Nine seasons

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.129
I had six coaches, counting interim coaches—
- Right.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:48.131
I had six coaches, counting interim coaches—
- Right.

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:49.716
- Yes.
- So all I know is turnover.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.259
- Yeah.
- And now to see the success

00:00:51.259 --> 00:00:52.886
of this group.
- Before you is the Greatest

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.471
Show on Turf.
- Yeah.

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:56.389
- After you is Sean McVay
and this offensive explosion.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.724
- Right.
- In-between—

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.809
- Yeah, I'm just the meat.
- Yeah.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:01.895
Well, I know.
So, so, I do.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.147
I mean, you're one of the great
running backs of all time.

00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:06.232
You're 18th on the all-time
rushing list.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.901
- Wild.
- Do you feel like

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.195
you're almost,
like, the forgotten man

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:12.447
not only as a whole,
but for the Rams?

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:14.199
Like, I feel like people
just go

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:16.326
"Marshall Faulk" and "Todd Gurley."

00:01:16.326 --> 00:01:18.578
And they forget that you were,
like, a super stud

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.038
in the NFL for a long time.

00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:22.457
- Yeah. Well, my
favorite question to fans

00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:24.375
that say they're real fans is,
"Who's the leading rusher

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:26.002
for the L.A. Rams?"
- Right.

00:01:26.002 --> 00:01:28.088
- Most people say Eric Dickerson.
It's like, well

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.381
you don't know your history.
You didn't watch me, obviously.

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:32.050
- Yeah.
- Right.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.676
- And that's the
frustrating part, is, you know

00:01:33.676 --> 00:01:35.178
I understand
that team leadership

00:01:35.178 --> 00:01:36.638
and team wins come together.

00:01:36.638 --> 00:01:38.056
And I just wasn't a part
of that team.

00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:39.599
- Right.
- But when you talk about

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.935
individual and what a person
put out on the field

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.311
what we worked hard to do?
- Yeah.

00:01:43.311 --> 00:01:44.771
- I just want
some acknowledgement.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.648
And sometimes I feel like
I get skipped over

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:48.316
and it's not because
of my talent.

00:01:48.316 --> 00:01:49.776
I know that.
It's just because

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.820
I just had a bad break, man.
- Yeah, yeah that's what happens.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.363
- Well, we talk about it
all the time.

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:55.824
It's everyone says
that wins isn't a statistic.

00:01:55.824 --> 00:01:57.242
But yet, we treat it like

00:01:57.242 --> 00:01:58.827
it's the greatest statistic
of all time.

00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:00.995
- You're right. Yeah.
- That's kinda how it goes.

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:03.414
But what's funny is,
is then you go to the Patriots

00:02:03.414 --> 00:02:06.626
which, there's nothing better
than Bill Belichick with a guy

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.254
that hasn't been getting respect
from another team.

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:11.047
Happened with Corey Dillon.
It happened with

00:02:11.047 --> 00:02:13.341
you know, like, every safety,
wide receivers.

00:02:13.341 --> 00:02:15.510
Happened with Chad Johnson,
our friend.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.595
You go there.

00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:19.889
What was your first meeting
with Belichick?

00:02:19.889 --> 00:02:21.641
Like, what were your—
what was a great

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.102
Belichick story
about who he really is?

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:27.313
- My story of Belichick
is he calls me in December

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.983
LeGarrette Blount goes down,
he gets hurt.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.651
- That was the injury.
- That was the injury.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:34.154
He goes down, and I'm retired
at this point in my head.

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.530
And it's Belichick.
You know that voice.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:36.823
It's very distinct.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:37.949
And he goes, "Steven—"
- "Hi, Steven."

00:02:37.949 --> 00:02:39.492
- Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.745
He goes, "Steven, uh, I got
a question for you.

00:02:42.745 --> 00:02:44.664
Do you wanna play
football again?"

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.999
And I'm like, in my head

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.834
like, "Of course I do."
- Yeah.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.627
- But I'm like,
they're in December.

00:02:49.627 --> 00:02:51.212
This is the
New England Patriots

00:02:51.212 --> 00:02:52.422
and I'm a man of pride.

00:02:52.422 --> 00:02:53.464
I don't wanna look bad.

00:02:53.464 --> 00:02:55.133
Like, the—my last carry

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.051
I felt I still
looked like myself.

00:02:57.051 --> 00:02:58.344
I didn't wanna get
to New England

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.596
and look like a shell of myself.

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:00.930
- Yeah.
- And then people are like

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.140
"Oh, he's—"
you know, "He's terrible.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:03.600
He's trash."
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.018
- So I was more nervous
about public opinion

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.394
about what I would look like.

00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:08.021
- Mmm.
- So I said, "Coach, you give me

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.315
two weeks to get in shape,
I'll come."

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:10.773
two weeks to get in shape,
I'll come."

00:03:10.773 --> 00:03:12.108
What was it
like going there

00:03:12.108 --> 00:03:13.693
seeing their day-to-day
preparation

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:17.155
and specifically, like,
AFC Championship

00:03:17.155 --> 00:03:19.240
getting ready for the Broncos
that year

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.533
what that was like being a part

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.160
of that organization
during that time?

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.786
- So, when you get there,
you realize that there's

00:03:23.786 --> 00:03:27.332
no place like it in the NFL,
at least my stops.

00:03:27.332 --> 00:03:30.043
There's not a lot of pictures
in the hallways.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:33.254
There's not a lot of
"me, me, me," you know?

00:03:33.254 --> 00:03:34.964
But what I found
the most interesting

00:03:34.964 --> 00:03:36.674
to your question, is getting
ready for that AFC game

00:03:36.674 --> 00:03:39.510
against the Denver Broncos,
if I recall right

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.095
he asked me to talk to the team.

00:03:41.095 --> 00:03:44.182
And he wanted me to talk to them
about my NFL experience.

00:03:44.182 --> 00:03:46.476
I'm like, "What do I have
to teach these guys," you know?

00:03:46.476 --> 00:03:48.937
You guys have been to now eight
consecutive AFC championships.

00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:50.647
- Right.
- Gronkowski's laughing.

00:03:50.647 --> 00:03:53.358
He goes, "I've never
had not a bye," right?

00:03:53.358 --> 00:03:54.984
- Right.
- I'm like, I've only been

00:03:54.984 --> 00:03:56.986
in the playoffs twice,
first year and last year.

00:03:56.986 --> 00:03:58.905
- Yeah.
- And he's laughing like

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.782
"You got a bad break."
- Right.

00:04:00.782 --> 00:04:02.909
- So he asked me to talk
about my plight

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.577
so I'm telling the team
about my story.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:08.039
And my story goes,
there's a part of my career

00:04:08.039 --> 00:04:10.667
where I won six games
in three years.

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:11.459
- Wow.

00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:14.003
I'm talking to the team
about me winning six games

00:04:14.003 --> 00:04:15.213
in three years.
- Yeah.

00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:16.506
- And you could just hear
a pin drop.

00:04:16.506 --> 00:04:17.632
And they just couldn't believe
the amount

00:04:17.632 --> 00:04:18.466
And they just couldn't believe
the amount

00:04:18.466 --> 00:04:20.051
of eight consecutive
1,000 yards rushing

00:04:20.051 --> 00:04:20.551
of eight consecutive
1,000 yards rushing

00:04:20.551 --> 00:04:22.762
but the lack of wins
to go with it.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:23.638
but the lack of wins
to go with it.

00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:27.183
It's almost like those guys
wanted to win that game for me.

00:04:27.183 --> 00:04:28.643
- Yeah.
- And that was a special moment

00:04:28.643 --> 00:04:28.810
- Yeah.
- And that was a special moment

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.104
because I didn't think
my story was anything.

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.855
I thought I was just privileged
to be there.

00:04:32.855 --> 00:04:35.149
But to see that it was twofold,
and that they wanted me

00:04:35.149 --> 00:04:38.069
to kinda cap off
my career with a win.

00:04:38.069 --> 00:04:39.570
- Sure.
- It meant a lot to me

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:41.406
and, you know,
I'll always forever be grateful.

00:04:41.406 --> 00:04:44.617
- And you got a touchdown in the
AFC Championship Game in Denver.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.869
- Do you think he was
trying to, like

00:04:46.869 --> 00:04:49.706
you know, Belichick,
like, is he trying to show, like

00:04:49.706 --> 00:04:51.332
"Hey, you guys are spoiled."
- Absolutely he was.

00:04:51.332 --> 00:04:53.167
- "And look how grateful
this—." Yeah, OK.

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:54.544
- You can't take it
for granted, right?

00:04:54.544 --> 00:04:55.128
- Right, right.
- And I think, if you're

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:55.503
- Right, right.
- And I think, if you're

00:04:55.503 --> 00:04:57.297
Gronkowski, for example,
he doesn't know anything else.

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.339
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:58.339 --> 00:04:59.674
- He only knows Brady, Belichick

00:04:59.674 --> 00:05:01.384
and playoff wins,
you know what I'm saying?

00:05:01.384 --> 00:05:03.803
- He assumes that Cincinnati's
like that.

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.138
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.431
- Now they're in
a similar situation.

00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:08.266
They haven't been
in that situation

00:05:08.266 --> 00:05:11.811
since your speech and that game
of a road AFC Championship Game.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:15.773
And since 2004, they've been to
the playoffs, like, 13 times.

00:05:15.773 --> 00:05:19.360
This has only happened three
times, and the Patriots are 0-3.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.195
- 0-3 on the road.
- I'm curious

00:05:21.195 --> 00:05:25.033
what is Belichick like the week
of an AFC Championship Game?

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:27.035
- Very relaxed. Everyone—
- Really?

00:05:27.035 --> 00:05:29.203
- And I would say the whole team.

00:05:29.203 --> 00:05:31.080
That's the, that was the other
thing that was impressive.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.791
From the running back coach
to the special teams coach

00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:35.543
to even just
the team chaplain, it is—

00:05:35.543 --> 00:05:38.129
- Nothing's different.
- Nothing's different there.

00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:39.672
It is normal.

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:42.133
Football in January and February
is normal to them.

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:43.634
- It's the regular season.
- Sounds like you were

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:45.428
in a bizarro world—
- I was.

00:05:45.428 --> 00:05:47.263
- Where you're like,
"I've never been here before.

00:05:47.263 --> 00:05:49.265
This is insane." And everyone's
like, "It's Tuesday, Steven.

00:05:49.265 --> 00:05:50.767
Take a seat."
- Yeah, I'm normally

00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:51.934
looking at my passport.

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:53.227
I'm in Costa Rica
somewhere, right?

00:05:53.227 --> 00:05:54.520
- Yeah.
- And they're like, "Nah, man.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.564
This is divisional round week."

00:05:56.564 --> 00:05:59.317
- My only other thing is

00:05:59.317 --> 00:06:04.655
if you could say anything to
the basketball Stephen Jackson

00:06:04.655 --> 00:06:06.866
what would you say to him?
- Stak5, what's up?

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:07.408
what would you say to him?
- Stak5, what's up?

00:06:07.408 --> 00:06:08.868
- Do you guys, like, talk?

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.286
Do the Steven Jacksons
talk to each other?

00:06:10.286 --> 00:06:11.788
- No, we haven't talked in a while.

00:06:11.788 --> 00:06:13.831
We've, we ran into
each other before.

00:06:13.831 --> 00:06:16.501
Um, oddly enough,
it was in a nightclub

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:19.712
in San Antonio and I—
we got each other's bills.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.339
- Really? That's how you—
Did you even—

00:06:21.339 --> 00:06:23.925
- You don't wanna mess with
that NBA money, man.

00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:25.343
- Yeah, yeah.
I'm like, no, no, no.

00:06:25.343 --> 00:06:26.719
I'm not guaranteed.
I'll take the small one.

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.054
- I didn't order three
Ace of Spades.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:29.722
- Right.
So there's been some mixups.

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.432
- That's unbelievable.
I love it.

00:06:31.432 --> 00:06:32.350
We're happy to have you, man.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:33.726
- Thank you, man.
- Yeah, thanks for coming by.

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.686
- For real.
- Seriously.

